# ContextUnity ACDD Documentation

**Augmented Context & Durable Dispatch (ACDD)** is a single pure-Rust binary (`MCP server` + `CLI`) that gives AI coding agents and developers an incremental Tree-sitter code graph, an architectural linter, and a deterministic gate state machine — 100% locally, with zero background daemons.

> [!TIP]
> **New to ACDD?** Start with the **[5-Minute Quickstart](/docs/getting-started/quickstart/)** to install the binary, index your repository, connect your AI agent, and run your first verified task.

---

## Adopt ACDD in three progressive steps

- **1. Smart Navigation & Linter (Zero Workflow Setup)**: Run `acdd init` and connect MCP. Agents immediately gain single-shot AST symbol reads (`acdd_read`), caller/blast-radius analysis (`code_map_impact`), BM25 docs search, and `acdd lint` boundary checks.
- **2. Guardrailed Ad-Hoc Tasks (`--goal`)**: Run `acdd start --goal "..." --profile hotfix` for bugfixes and small features — enforcing write scopes, automated test checks, and independent review without authoring a spec file.
- **3. Multi-Wave Specs & Parallel Agents**: Draft versioned specs (`acdd draft`), synthesize per-task architectural slices, and coordinate parallel builder and reviewer subagents across isolated Git `.worktrees/`.

---

